# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The server is compiled to a real .exe in-tree, and a .syso produced by
# rsrc/goversioninfo is architecture- and toolchain-specific. Neither belongs in
# history: the .syso in particular is regenerated by the documented build step,
# so committing it would make every other checkout fail to link on a different
# Go/Windows combination.
*.exe
*.exe~
*.syso
server/smart-remote-app.exe
server/smart-remote-test.exe

# Flutter / Dart
mobile/build/
mobile/.dart_tool/
mobile/.flutter-plugins
mobile/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
mobile/.packages
mobile/pubspec.lock
mobile/**/generated_plugin_registrant.dart
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/local.properties
mobile/android/app/debug/
mobile/android/app/profile/
mobile/android/app/release/
mobile/ios/Pods/
mobile/ios/.symlinks/
mobile/ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
mobile/ios/Flutter/Flutter.podspec
mobile/ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
mobile/ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh
mobile/macos/Pods/
mobile/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
mobile/linux/flutter/ephemeral/

# Go
server/vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The server writes its own log next to the binary. It is machine-specific and
# can grow without bound, and it records the pairing PIN in plain text, so it
# must never be committed.
*.log
config/macros.json

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Release artefacts. These are copied out of mobile/build after a release build
# so they are easy to find and sideload, but a 50MB APK per commit bloats the
# history without adding anything a rebuild cannot reproduce.
release.apk
server/smart-remote-app.exe
server/smart-remote-test.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal scratch files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are local notes kept by hand, not build output. They are ignored
# explicitly by name so a broad cleanup glob can never sweep them up.
_f.txt
_flutter.txt
server/_s.txt
mobile/_analyze.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test / coverage artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
*.coverprofile